  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 909 PM MST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nHigh pressure will persist through the week, bringing warmer and \ndrier conditions. Temperatures are expected to run 5-10 degrees \nabove normal through at least Friday, with mostly clear skies. A \nquick moving system to our north will bring increased cloud cover on \nTuesday afternoon, as well as maybe some breezy winds across \nnortheast Utah and northwest Colorado. Otherwise, expect sunny skies \nand light winds. \n\nModels indicate a deep trough developing off the West Coast by the \nend of the week, which has the potential to bring a shift to cooler \nand wetter conditions over eastern Utah and western Colorado for the \ncoming weekend. Model agreement remains poor this far out, so be \nsure to stay tuned to see how the forecast develops over the coming \ndays.",
